# The image is one binary: `COPY minecraft_pinger /bin/minecraft_pinger`. Everything else in the
# context is build residue, and the context is on the NFS workspace PVC, so `target/` (a few hundred
# MB of .rlib and incremental junk) would be walked and shipped to the daemon for nothing.
#
# The `*` then allow-one-file form is deliberate: adding a file to the Dockerfile later has to be an
# explicit change here, not an accident that quietly grows the context.
*
!minecraft_pinger
